563		<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
564			<section aria-label="Introduction">
565				<p>This is a well-structured, accessible HTML5 document demonstrating modern best practices for semantic markup and inclusive design.</p>
566				<p>
567					It uses semantic landmarks, a skip link for keyboard navigation,
568					and CSS that adapts to your light or dark mode preference.
569				</p>
570				<p>
571					Text and link colors meet WCAG AA contrast in both themes, type scales
572					with your browser's font size, and motion respects your system settings.
573				</p>
574			</section>
575	
576			<section aria-labelledby="features">
577				<h2 id="features">Features</h2>
578				<ul>
579					<li>Semantic HTML structure with proper landmarks</li>
580					<li>Keyboard accessible navigation and focus management</li>
581					<li>Dark mode support with custom color schemes</li>
582					<li>Responsive typography using modern CSS</li>
583					<li>Print-friendly styles for better readability</li>
584					<li>WCAG AA contrast compliance in all color modes</li>
585				</ul>
586			</section>
587	
588			<section aria-labelledby="examples">
589				<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>
590				<article class="card">
591					<h3>Component Cards</h3>
592					<p>Card components are useful for organizing related content. They include a subtle border and padding for visual separation.</p>
593					<a class="button" href="#resources">Learn more<span class="visually-hidden"> about accessibility resources</span></a>
594				</article>
595	
596				<article class="card">
597					<h3>Interactive Elements</h3>
598					<p>Buttons and links are fully accessible with clear focus states. All interactive elements include visible focus indicators and proper ARIA labels.</p>
599					<p><strong>Keyboard navigation:</strong> Use <kbd>Tab</kbd> to move forward, <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd> to move backward, and <kbd>Enter</kbd> or <kbd>Space</kbd> to activate.</p>
600				</article>
601	
602				<article class="card">
603					<h3>Accessible Form</h3>
604					<form id="contact-form" novalidate>
605						<p class="form-hint">Fields marked * are required.</p>
606						<div class="field">
607							<label for="email">Email <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
608							<input type="email" id="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" inputmode="email" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="none" required aria-describedby="email-help">
609							<span id="email-error" class="error-message" aria-live="polite"></span>
610							<small id="email-help" class="form-hint">For example, name@example.com</small>
611						</div>
612						<div class="field">
613							<label for="message">Message</label>
614							<textarea id="message" name="message" rows="4" maxlength="2000" aria-describedby="message-help"></textarea>
615							<small id="message-help" class="form-hint">Up to 2,000 characters. <span id="message-count">2,000</span> remaining.</small>
616						</div>
617						<button type="submit">Send message</button>
618						<p id="form-status" role="status"></p>
619					</form>
620				</article>
621	
622				<article class="card">
623					<h3>Live Region Example</h3>
624					<p>Click the button to announce a message using a live region. This demonstrates how screen readers are notified of dynamic updates.</p>
625					<button id="announce" type="button">Announce message</button>
626					<div class="live-region" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
627						<span id="live-message"></span>
628					</div>
629				</article>
